{
  "id": "r08",
  "text": "In this September twenty nineteen investigation, McDonald changes how P.T. handles objects that appear and disappear. Watch the ordinary encounter first: Lisa is visible down the hallway, then she's gone. Now look at the altered version. Her visibility stays on, and the camera can approach a model the normal sequence only lets you glimpse. This isn't another person recreating the house. It's an investigation of the original software and the instructions controlling what the player can see. McDonald also examines the opening room. The normal opening directs your attention through a narrow view of the doorway. By changing the way that moment runs, he can inspect the character model outside it. The point isn't that a hidden model automatically changes the plot. It's that a recording of one playthrough cannot contain every possible investigation of the program that produced it. The cancellation had already happened. The advertising campaign was over. Yet the surviving teaser still had details that somebody could reveal by asking a new question of the same old software.",
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural",
  "rate": "+0%",
  "pitch": "+0Hz",
